Total IP Control v2.0.0
Copyright (c) 2026 Sysop Network

Total IP Control restores real caller IPs from a reverse proxy, enforces
per-IP connection limits, records caller IPs and GeoIP locations to user
profiles, and keeps a full audit trail -- all set up live from the BBS.

  This release replaces ALL FOUR files: SNTIPCTL.DLL, SNTIPCTL.MSG,
  SNTIPCTL.MDF and SNTIPCTL.RLN. Install them together.


What is new in 2.0.0:
  * /TIP replaces /TOTALIP and the old full-screen forms. Settings are
    in six sections (General, Telnet Trusted Proxies, IPv4 Whitelist,
    IPv6 Whitelist, GeoIP Location, SSH Settings). Pick a section, pick
    a setting by number, type the new value. Every change applies and
    saves at once and leaves an Audit Trail line. ? explains a setting,
    H is a quick-start guide, X goes back.

  * The same menu opens from a BBS menu item whose command line is:

       MENU=SYSOPMENU

    Give the item a Sysop key. MASTER access is needed, as for /TIP.

  * 10 trusted proxies each for telnet and SSH, and 50-entry IPv4 and
    IPv6 whitelists (10 to a page; N and P turn the page).

  * Full IPv6 caller support behind a proxy (PROXY TCP6): the real IPv6
    address is used by /MYIP, /WHOSON, the logs, GeoIP, the connection
    limit and the user profile. Trusted proxies stay IPv4 -- the BBS
    listens on IPv4, so the proxy always reaches it over IPv4.

  * SSH: its own trusted-proxy policy and PROXY header support, set up
    separately from telnet (off until you turn it on).

  * /MYIP shows any caller their real IP. /WHOSON shows staff who is on,
    with connection type, real IP, module and time on line.

  * Text variables for your own messages: N!SNTIP, N!SNTIPSHORT,
    N!SNTUSERID, N!SNTMODULE, N!SNTTOL, N!SNTTIPCT, N!SNTVER.

  * Debug trace log (General Settings) for troubleshooting, written to
    TOTALIPCONTROL\DEBUG\.

Fixed since 1.1.2:
  * A board crash (OVERSIZED SPR() CALL) when the module gateway refused
    a user while several users were on from the same IP.
  * Real IPs lost while WorldLink was connected.
  * SSH connections through a PROXY front end failing intermittently.
  * Every refused connection froze the board for half a second; the
    refusal message is now also delivered reliably.
  * Log writing could stall the board; log files are now kept open.


Installing:
  1. Stop the BBS.
  2. Copy SNTIPCTL.DLL, SNTIPCTL.MSG, SNTIPCTL.MDF and SNTIPCTL.RLN into
     your BBS installation directory (typically C:\BBSV10), replacing
     any older copies.
  3. Remove PROXCLIP and IPControl (IPCTRL) if you still run them.
  4. Restart. The Audit Trail at start-up reports v2.0.0.
  5. Type /TIP as a Master user and set it up.

Upgrading from 1.x:
  Your settings carry over unchanged. Every message in SNTIPCTL.MSG is
  new, so if you reworded any Total IP Control message (CLIMIT, PRXBLK,
  IPGDNY, ...) in the message editor, note your text before installing
  and redo it afterwards. In CLIMIT and IPGDNY use N!SNTUSERS where %s
  was and N!SNTMAXIP where %d was.

Load order (wgserv.cfg):
  SNTIPCTL must load after GALTNTD, and after SNSSH if you use SSH. The
  usual alphabetical order already does this; if not, the Audit Trail
  says so at start-up.


